diff --git a/api-ref/source/server-checkpoints.inc b/api-ref/source/server-checkpoints.inc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..396e7ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/api-ref/source/server-checkpoints.inc
@@ -0,0 +1,238 @@
+.. -*- rst -*-
+
+=========================================
+Server checkpoints (private N1 extension)
+=========================================
+
+All routes in this section require microversion ``2.106`` in this fork.
+N1 implements a durable model, not a working production RAM snapshot engine.
+The production executor reports unsupported until N2 and backend validation
+are delivered. The successful examples below were captured from real Nova
+WSGI/RPC tests using a test-only executor.
+
+Project readers may inspect their server's resources; project members may
+mutate them. Authorization is checked again for idempotent retries. System
+scope and a different project cannot access these resources. Requests reject
+unknown body/query fields. Host/path information, tokens and raw backend
+evidence are never returned.
+
+Mutation responses are ``202 Accepted``. Poll the operation UUID for the
+current result. Request UUIDs are unique within a project/server across all
+three actions. Exact retries by the same actor and with the same action and
+payload resolve to the original operation. Conflicting reuse returns ``409``.
+A retry does not authorize re-execution of a claimed destructive step.
+Timeouts do not imply cancellation or quota refund.
+
+Inspect checkpoint capabilities
+===============================
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /servers/{server_id}/checkpoint-capabilities
+
+Report live executor support for this server. A supported service/RPC version
+alone does not prove support. When creation is disabled, the response has
+``supported: false``, ``reasons: ["disabled"]`` and ``profile: null``.
+
+Normal response codes: 200
+
+Error response codes: badRequest(400), forbidden(403), itemNotFound(404),
+conflict(409), serviceUnavailable(503)
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - server_id: server_id_path
+  - capabilities: checkpoint_capabilities
+  - supported: checkpoint_supported
+  - reasons: checkpoint_reasons
+  - profile: checkpoint_profile
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/capabilities.json
+   :language: json
+
+Create a checkpoint
+===================
+
+.. rest_method:: POST /servers/{server_id}/checkpoints
+
+Request one independent point including runtime memory and all supported
+writable disks. Disk subsets and memory-free checkpoints are not accepted.
+New create is denied when disabled, the executor is unsupported, identity has
+changed, ownership is busy or the count/byte budget is exhausted. The default
+byte budget is zero. Pending work and incomplete cleanup remain charged.
+
+Normal response codes: 202
+
+Error response codes: badRequest(400), forbidden(403), itemNotFound(404),
+conflict(409), overLimit(413), serviceUnavailable(503)
+
+Request
+-------
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - server_id: server_id_path
+  - checkpoint: checkpoint_request_body
+  - request_id: checkpoint_request_id
+  - name: checkpoint_name_request
+  - include_memory: checkpoint_include_memory
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/create-req.json
+   :language: json
+
+Response
+--------
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - checkpoint: checkpoint_body
+  - operation: checkpoint_operation_body
+
+The checkpoint can already be available when the HTTP response arrives.
+The included operation is an acceptance projection; read its resource for
+the latest state. These two projections are not an atomic state snapshot.
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/create-resp.json
+   :language: json
+
+List checkpoints
+================
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /servers/{server_id}/checkpoints
+
+List retained points ordered by creation time and UUID. Deleted tombstones
+are omitted. A marker must belong to the same server; a deleted point remains
+a valid marker. No cross-server or cross-cell list is exposed.
+
+Normal response codes: 200
+
+Error response codes: badRequest(400), forbidden(403), itemNotFound(404),
+serviceUnavailable(503)
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - server_id: server_id_path
+  - limit: checkpoint_limit
+  - marker: checkpoint_marker
+  - checkpoints: checkpoints_body
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/list-resp.json
+   :language: json
+
+Show a checkpoint
+=================
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /servers/{server_id}/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}
+
+Show one retained point. A deleted checkpoint returns ``404``; its operation
+history remains addressable while the server is addressable.
+
+Normal response codes: 200
+
+Error response codes: badRequest(400), forbidden(403), itemNotFound(404),
+serviceUnavailable(503)
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - server_id: server_id_path
+  - checkpoint_id: checkpoint_id_path
+  - checkpoint: checkpoint_body
+  - id: checkpoint_id_body
+  - server_id: checkpoint_server_id
+  - name: checkpoint_name_body
+  - status: checkpoint_status
+  - created_at: checkpoint_created_at
+  - operation_id: checkpoint_active_operation
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/show-resp.json
+   :language: json
+
+Revert to a checkpoint
+======================
+
+.. rest_method:: POST /servers/{server_id}/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}/action
+
+Restore the same server's runtime and disk contents without replacing its
+server/volume/port UUIDs. This does not restore IP leases, security groups or
+other external network state. A new revert still requires a supported live
+probe, even when new creation is disabled. Partial or unknown results retain
+ownership and prevent an unsafe guest restart; there is no force option.
+
+Normal response codes: 202
+
+Error response codes: badRequest(400), forbidden(403), itemNotFound(404),
+conflict(409), overLimit(413), serviceUnavailable(503)
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - server_id: server_id_path
+  - checkpoint_id: checkpoint_id_path
+  - revert: checkpoint_revert_body
+  - request_id: checkpoint_request_id
+  - operation: checkpoint_operation_body
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/revert-req.json
+   :language: json
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/action-resp.json
+   :language: json
+
+Delete a checkpoint
+===================
+
+.. rest_method:: DELETE /servers/{server_id}/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}
+
+Supply ``OpenStack-Checkpoint-Request-ID`` with a client-generated UUID.
+Delete has no request body. Completion requires proof of resource deletion;
+quota remains charged while resources or an uncertain result remain. Deleting
+one point must preserve the others. New delete remains available when new
+creation is disabled, subject to live executor support and ownership checks.
+An exact replay after deletion resolves to the original operation.
+
+Normal response codes: 202
+
+Error response codes: badRequest(400), forbidden(403), itemNotFound(404),
+conflict(409), overLimit(413), serviceUnavailable(503)
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - server_id: server_id_path
+  - checkpoint_id: checkpoint_id_path
+  - OpenStack-Checkpoint-Request-ID: checkpoint_request_header
+  - operation: checkpoint_operation_body
+
+Read an operation
+=================
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /servers/{server_id}/checkpoint-operations/{operation_id}
+
+Read the durable operation's public projection. ``recovery_required`` is an
+unresolved outcome, not permission to repeat effects or clear ownership.
+Disabling the feature does not remove existing read or recovery paths.
+
+Normal response codes: 200
+
+Error response codes: badRequest(400), forbidden(403), itemNotFound(404),
+serviceUnavailable(503)
+
+.. rest_parameters:: parameters.yaml
+
+  - server_id: server_id_path
+  - operation_id: checkpoint_operation_path
+  - operation: checkpoint_operation_body
+  - id: checkpoint_operation_id
+  - checkpoint_id: checkpoint_id_body
+  - kind: checkpoint_operation_kind
+  - state: checkpoint_operation_state
+  - phase: checkpoint_operation_phase
+  - error_code: checkpoint_error_code
+  - created_at: checkpoint_created_at
+  - updated_at: checkpoint_updated_at
+
+Completed revert:
+
+.. literalinclude:: samples/server-checkpoints/operation-resp.json
+   :language: json
+
+Completed delete after resource proof and quota release:
+
