+---
+features:
+  - |
+    This fork adds the private instance checkpoint model at Compute API
+    microversion 2.106: a cell-local durable operation journal, project-wide
+    count/byte reservations, ownership guards and reconciliation. Production
+    executors remain unsupported. RAM and Cinder effects require the separate
+    N2 implementation and backend/runtime validation.
+upgrade:
+  - |
+    Apply API DB migration 71be90d2c402 and cell DB migration 4a8c2d7e9101
+    before running the new writers. Future activation requires every writer
+    to be upgraded, compute RPC 6.5, compute-task RPC 1.26, service version 69
+    and a supported live executor probe. Mixed-writer activation is unsupported.
+    The default is disabled, with limits of 8 checkpoints per instance,
+    100 per project and zero artifact bytes; zero denies creation.
+security:
+  - |
+    Checkpoint request replay rechecks project authorization. Internal owner
+    tokens never enter public responses or notification contexts. Recovery
+    does not persist or impersonate the requesting user's token. Timeouts,
+    disabling creation and administrative state reset do not release durable
+    ownership or reserved quota. No force-unlock or ordinary-worker takeover
+    is provided by N1.
